.","dna16":"8800074131000424","ex":["In mathematics, an iterated function is a function which is composed with itself, possibly ad infinitum, in a process called iteration."],"id":"wikt:iterate:verb:4","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"To repeat an activity, making incremental changes each time.","dna16":"8800074131000523","ex":[],"id":"wikt:iterate:verb:5","pos":"verb","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[],"tags":["ambitransitive"]},{"def":"An n-fold self-composition of a function.","dna16":"8800074131000622","ex":[],"id":"wikt:iterate:noun:6","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"","syn":[]},{"def":"The image of a certain value under such a function.","dna16":"8800074131000721","ex":["f²(x₀) is the second iterate of x₀ under f."],"id":"wikt:iterate:noun:7","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"40:1,104:1","syn":[]}]},"iterated":{"dna16":"8800695006000014","forms_of":["iterate"],"senses":[]},"iterated function system":{"dna16":"8800695007000013","senses":[{"def":"A collection of transformations, which, when applied sequentially, can be used to construct a fractal. Formally: a finite set (or tuple) of contraction mappings on a complete metric space.","dna16":"8800695007000120","ex":[],"id":"wikt:iterated function system:noun:1","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"4:1,12:1,55:1,84:1,86:1","syn":[]}]},"iterated function systems":{"dna16":"8800695008000012","forms_of":["iterated function system"],"senses":[]},"iterated integral":{"dna16":"8800695009000011","senses":[{"def":"In multivariable calculus, the result of applying integrals to a function of more than one variable in such a way that each of the integrals considers some of the variables as given constants.","dna16":"8800695009000128","ex":[],"id":"wikt:iterated integral:noun:1","pos":"noun","src":"wikt","sym":"85:1","syn":[]}]},"iterated integrals":{"dna16":"8800695010000018","forms_of":["iterated integral"],"senses":[]},"iteratee":{"dna16":"8800695011000017","senses":[{"def":"In functional programming, a composa